/security-review — loop U4, round 2, range 31fcdb7..9fdb22f

No high-confidence vulnerabilities found.

The `code:sec` split does not remove or weaken any scan compared with `31fcdb7:tools/base/.config/mise/tasks/code/sec`. Each scanner command is the same, with the same flags and config path: gitleaks `git --staged` and gitleaks `dir` over the git-known files copied to a temp folder, both with `--redact 50`; grype with the same submodule excludes; osv-scanner with the same escaped regex excludes and `--allow-no-lockfiles`.

The pack `base` always includes `p:security`, so every consumer gets the three scanners and `_security_base`. The `sec` hook is unchanged: `mise x -- mise run code:sec --staged`, `always_run = true`.

The orchestrator now exits 1 when `code:sec:gitleaks`, `code:sec:grype` or `code:sec:osv-scanner` is missing or not executable (commit 94c87f8), and `set -e` stops it when any scanner fails. In staged mode grype and osv-scanner still exit 0, as before.

The scanners now run in the order gitleaks, grype, osv-scanner. Before, gitleaks ran last and a grype failure skipped it, so the new order is slightly stronger. The three scanner config files were already seeds in `tools/base/tools.toml` at 31fcdb7, so who owns them has not changed.

